# ai-budget-front

### 1. COMPACT & ACCURATE CODE

- Write small, focused functions
- Avoid unnecessary abstractions
- Keep code simple and readable
- Don't create extra layers unless absolutely necessary
- Prefer inline solutions over separate utilities

### 2. README.md

- Keep all info about start/setup project in it. Add to it env example without variables.

### 3. General

- Always refer to `.cursor/frontend-backend-spec.en.md` and `.cursor/backend-spec.md` for schema, naming, and business logic before generating backend-facing code.
- When implementing new features or significant changes, update `.cursor/frontend-spec.en.md` so it stays accurate.
- For existing HTTP routes and params, use `docs/api-routes.json` (keep English descriptions; align with `.cursor/backend-spec.md` when in doubt).

### 4. COMMENTS FOR COMPLEX LOGIC

- For non-trivial methods or functions, add a short description (docblock or inline comment) of what the method does or what a block of code is for.
- Prefer one line; avoid obvious restatements of the code.

### 5. Styles

- Don't use dark theme. We have only one bright theme.

### 5. Language

- For all namings in description, labels and so on use only english as primary language.
- Use for all namings that we have on the project vocabular.

### 6. ONLY absolute pathers for imports

- Use only absolute path, not relative.
